@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About RatPDF — Online PDF Tools & Document Utilities";
    ViewData["Description"] = "RatPDF provides free and Pro PDF tools: compress, merge, convert PDF to Word, Excel, and more. Learn how we process files securely and what makes our converters different.";
}

<head>
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow">
</head>

<article class="container my-5">
    <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm p-4 p-md-5" style="border-radius: 16px;">
        <h1 class="fw-bold mb-3">About RatPDF</h1>
        <p class="lead text-muted">
            RatPDF is a document productivity platform for individuals, freelancers, and small businesses
            who need reliable PDF workflows without installing desktop software.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mt-4">What we offer</h2>
        <p>
            The site combines <strong>40+ browser-accessible tools</strong> in one place: compress and merge PDFs,
            convert between PDF, Word, and Excel, extract text, add watermarks, protect files with passwords,
            and generate business documents such as invoices and payslips.
        </p>
        <p>
            Heavy conversions (PDF↔Office, OCR, Ghostscript compression) run on our cloud servers using
            open-source engines including <strong>pdf2docx</strong>, <strong>PyMuPDF</strong>, <strong>LibreOffice</strong>,
            <strong>Ghostscript</strong>, and <strong>iText</strong>. Lighter utilities may run entirely in your browser.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mt-4">Why we built it</h2>
        <p>
            Most “free PDF converters” strip tables, drop logos, or fail on scanned documents.
            RatPDF was designed around <em>layout fidelity</em>: when a bank statement, GST invoice, or client proposal
            must look correct in Word or Excel, our multi-engine pipeline tries structured extraction first and
            falls back to high-resolution page rendering when necessary.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mt-4">How file processing works</h2>
        <ol>
            <li>You upload a file over encrypted HTTPS.</li>
            <li>Our servers process it in an isolated job (temporary disk + optional Azure Blob storage for download).</li>
            <li>You receive a download link; background jobs delete stale files automatically.</li>
            <li>We do not sell uploaded documents or use them for advertising profiling.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
            Read the full details in our <a href="/Home/Privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mt-4">Free and Pro plans</h2>
        <p>
            Core tools remain free with daily limits (3 uses per tool, 200 MB per file).
            <a href="/Subscription/Plans">Pro subscribers</a> get unlimited conversions, 4 GB uploads, and
            high-fidelity Office conversions suited to agency and finance teams.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mt-4">Editorial content</h2>
        <p>
            Beyond one-click tools, we publish practical guides — for example
            <a href="/guides/compress-pdf-guide">how to compress PDFs without visible quality loss</a> and
            <a href="/guides/pdf-txt-guide">extracting text from scanned documents</a> — written for real
            office workflows, not keyword stuffing.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h4 fw-semibold mt-4">Contact &amp; feedback</h2>
        <p>
            Feature requests and bug reports help us prioritize engine upgrades and new tools.
            Reach us via the <a href="/Home/Contact">contact page</a>.
        </p>
    </div>
</article>
